From e1c5d767b4530d9509d4fa2378d519ace2678311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:36:36 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Interface: a waiting screen, Network page rows for ports,
 shared router addresses

For a port's online play:

- ui::wait_over_game(): a band over the last game frame while the game
  cannot go on (a network game waiting for the other player). The game
  stands still behind it as behind the paused menu. Holding back for a
  second leaves, with a bar that fills; a view with OK is a notice.
  Layer::escape_held() says whether Esc is down, since Esc never reaches
  ImGui.
- ui::add_network_rows(): a port's own rows on the Network page, after
  Ad hoc play's and before Status, as add_menu_rows() does for Video.
- RouterStatus::shared and router_wire::shared_address(): a router whose
  own outside address is private, provider-shared (100.64.0.0/10) or
  missing sits behind another, so opened ports reach nobody. The log and
  the Network page say so instead of offering that address.
- <PREFIX>_EXAMPLE_ADDRESSES=1 shows documentation addresses (RFC 5737)
  instead of real ones, for pictures of the page.
- The hosting rows no longer send players to "the Online Guild Hall",
  one game's name for its lobby.

Tested with Dissidia 012's port on Windows 11 (clang): the waiting band
and its hold to leave, a notice with OK, the input delay row on the
Network page and the example addresses, all seen in window captures;
adhoc_tests --router-messages passes under MSVC, with the address ranges.

Not tested: a router that really reports a shared address; the band on
macOS or Linux.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
